Upstream targets the reMarkable Paper Pro (aarch64, 1620x2160). Changes made
here for the reMarkable 2 (armv7 ILP32, 1404x1872, Qt 6.5.2):

  * qtfb_common.h  - wire structs pinned to the aarch64 layout with
                     static_assert on every offset. Upstream relies on natural
                     struct layout; `size_t shmSize` is 8 bytes on aarch64 but
                     4 on armv7, which silently breaks the handshake.
  * FBController   - RenderTarget::Image (the i.MX7 has no 3D GPU);
                     setActiveFocusOnTab instead of setFocusPolicy (Qt 6.7+);
                     update() is given an explicit bounding rect, because
                     update(QRect()) is a no-op while the dirty rect is empty.
  * fbmanagement   - MSG_NOSIGNAL so a dying client cannot SIGPIPE xochitl;
                     wildcard re-keying, since there is no AppLoad on this
                     device to agree a framebuffer key in advance.
  * screenmode.*   - NEW. Parents an EPScreenMode item onto the overlay so
                     xochitl selects the fast e-ink waveform for our region.
  * entry.cpp      - NEW. xovi entry point; attaches to the QQuickWindow's
                     contentItem from C++, so no QML patching is required.
